# Conventions

> Canonical, language-agnostic conventions for this project. This is what makes
> output consistent across IDEs and people.

## Code
- Keep changes small and focused; no drive-by refactors.
- Match the existing style of the file you are editing.
- Prefer clear names over comments; comment only non-obvious intent.
- Handle errors explicitly; never swallow exceptions silently.
- No secrets in code or config; use environment variables.

## Project layout
- Navigate via the generated code index, not by globbing the tree.
- New code goes in the module that owns its responsibility; create a new module
  only when none fits.

## Testing
- Test framework: **{{ conventions.test_framework }}**.
- Every behaviour change ships with a test.
- Name tests after the behaviour, not the function.

## Git
- Commit style: **{{ conventions.commit_style }}**.
- One logical change per commit.

## Reviews
- 🔴 Critical (must fix), 🟡 Suggestion, 🟢 Nice-to-have.
